; onehotr_row_out_of_range: a row outside the grid extent must raise.
;
; The only row of a 1x4 grid is row 0. `usize::try_from(row)` accepted any
; positive row, and `row * cols` then wrapped: 2^62 * 4 is exactly 0 modulo
; a 64-bit usize, so the Rust VM wrote a clean-looking one-hot constraint
; onto row 0 and halted successfully under `release` while it panicked
; under `ci-test` and xqvm_py raised. This vector pins IndexOutOfBounds on
; both implementations and on every profile.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 1           ; rows
PUSH 4           ; cols
RESIZE r0

PUSH 4611686018427387904   ; row == 2^62; row * cols wraps to 0
PUSH 1                     ; penalty
ONEHOTR r0
HALT
